  "rationale": "C wins narrowly over A. Its strengths: the clearest ranking, the closest reuse of existing conventions (tokens unchanged, the button's explicit-property pattern, its 80ms Reduced Motion value), concrete declarations an implementer can apply, and full restraint on the high-frequency palette. A has the deepest drag diagnosis but ranks less sharply, is padded by a speculative projection section, and ignores the local Reduced Motion precedent. B is competent, but its prioritization is undifferentiated and it keeps a palette animation on a keyboard-critical surface.",
