      "score": 81,
      "summary": "Solid recon and honest evidence labels. Plans have excerpts, boundaries, drift stops and 'to perform' runtime checks, and Reduced Motion reuses the 80ms precedent. It is weaker in three places. It keeps a token-timed palette entrance on the most keyboard-heavy surface, which is less restrained. Four of the five findings are P1, so ranking is weak. The drag plan skips velocity and release-continuity detail and only proposes a shorter settle. The toast plan's conditional translateY swap is reasonable but stays vague."
