      "score": 89,
      "summary": "Thorough and honest about what static evidence can show. It has a 'vetted out' list and the strongest drag diagnosis: coordinate model, grab offset, scroll, velocity handoff, re-grab cancellation and transform ownership. Reduced Motion is careful and never blanket-resets placement transforms. Weaknesses: the momentum-projection aside adds length, the priority tiers barely differ (nearly everything is P2), and the button's 80ms Reduced Motion precedent goes unused. The response is also dense and likely over the 180-line budget."
