      "score": 92,
      "summary": "Well-balanced and the most ready to implement. Priorities are ranked by location with a clear 'not promoted' list, and the palette animation is removed outright rather than re-tuned. It gives concrete token-based CSS declarations and preserves transforms owned by positioning. Its Reduced Motion rules copy the button's 80ms precedent exactly. The drag plan captures the rendered position before setDragging resets styling and handles stale callbacks. It covers drag velocity less than A does, but every plan has exact excerpts, boundaries, checks and drift stops."
